  }
  .safety-callout.safety-callout p + p { margin-top: 14px; }
  /* The aside's opening eyebrow (`calloutEyebrow`). The type itself is the
     shared `.eyebrow` rule above — the page sheets' base eyebrow restated
     token for token (all-on-4-single-arch.css:352 relies on the same base).
     The dash pair on `.section-head .eyebrow` is deliberately NOT reproduced:
     it is the centred section-head treatment, and inside this left-aligned
     cream box a dash would hang against the text. `display: block` puts the
     `<h3>` on its own line; the 14px gap is `.compare-sub-head h3`'s
     `margin: 14px 0 0` (all-on-4-single-arch.css:362-366) carried by the
     eyebrow instead, because the aside's h3 already owns its bottom margin.
     Colour restated for the same R2 reason as the h3/p rules above: the box
     is cream on EVERY band, and the (0,3,0) band recolours earlier in this
     sheet would otherwise win the tie and paint the eyebrow pale on charcoal
     cream. Doubled class so the tie is ours by source order, same lever as
     the two rules above. */
  .safety-callout.safety-callout .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  /* No link rule here on purpose. An `<a class="vs-link">` arriving through
