     identical lever and the identical margin the `.safety-callout` rules run on,
     so the two behave the same way rather than one of them being special.

     global.css:228-249 also lists `.config-card.config-card` in the sitewide
     white-card rescue at (0,3,1), which would catch this anyway — but a block
     whose text colour depends on a global sheet it does not own is not
     droppable on an arbitrary page (R3), so it is settled here.

     `line-height: 1.1` and `margin: 0` come from the page sheets' h1-h4 group
     rule (all-on-4-single-arch.css:39-42), collapsed to what actually renders —
     the flex `gap` above is the only spacing this card is meant to have. */
  .config-card.config-card h4 {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 22px;
